WEBVTT

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:10.990
Sleep, sleep peacefully, my child.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:20.400
For you are a dear boy, a really good child. Enjoy thy slumber.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:30.680
Little boy, bear in mind, whichever path you may take,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.990
Are you ready?!

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.570
Not yet ~nano desu!

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:40.210
once we pass through the mountains, we shall be at the village.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.260
How come there's a shrine here?

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:50.310
On your return to the village, be wary of which path you take,

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.240
Are you ready?!

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:58.940
for you may run into a demon.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.190
I'm ready!

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.030
I'm ready!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:05.340
Happy! Lucky! Which way? Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.370
Happy! Lucky! Which way? No! No! No!

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:13.430
Happy! Lucky! Which way? Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.290
Happy! Lucky! Which way? No! No! No!

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:21.110
There's something I want to tell you.

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:25.360
It's a secret.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.740
Hey, hey! That's no good.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:33.410
I don't like scary stories.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:37.480
I'm going to cast my magic.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.500
...over even the creepy path you always take home.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.630
Over short-cuts, the path to the stage, and our secret base.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.670
It's simple. Very, very easy! (Let's go!)

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.810
Swing straight ahead. Happy! Lucky! (1, 2, 3!)

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:57.930
Girls, take a peek into your hearts. (Come on!)

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.960
Smiling by accident, my heart races and melts. (1, 2, 3!)

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.080
This way? Just kidding. Which way was it, again? (Come on!)

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.570
You know, the answer is that I L-O-V-E you!

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:14.660
Happy! Lucky! Which way? Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:18.750
Happy! Lucky! Which way? No! No! No!

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.830
Happy! Lucky! Which way? Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:27.140
Happy! Lucky! Which way? No! No! No!

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.580
Tale of the Dream Painting

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.980
Rika?

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.480
Satoko?

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.400
Rika?!

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.150
Satoko?!

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.700
To Hanyuu:

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.900
You looked so peaceful when you were sleeping, that we went without waking you.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.790
Satoko and I are doing our homework at Mii-chan's place.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.050
We'll be back before nightfall.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:01.430
It looks like today is going to be really hot.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.320
Even though it's already September.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.450
Now that I'm alone for a change, I have no idea what to do.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.040
If I went to Mion's place, I could meet them...

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.810
There's no mistaking this voice!

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:02.920
Hanyuu?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.850
Erm...

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.970
You're Hanyuu, right?

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.040
No. I'm not!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.540
I don't even know who this Hanyuu person you are talking about is.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:20.660
But your face looks exactly like hers, and the way you talk...

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.300
That's because... we just look alike.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.870
It's a huge coincidence ~nano desu!

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.470
Good day to you.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:51.330
A good day to you, too!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.430
So you're not actually Hanyuu.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.020
Because only I can see Hanyuu.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.480
And I can't touch her.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:20.780
I'm glad you finally understand.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.490
May I ask you what your name is?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.490
Furude Rika.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:28.640
So it <i>is</i> her.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.240
You're lost, right?

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.630
I am lost.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.100
I understand.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.810
I'll take you home, then.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:39.410
Really?

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:46.200
Protecting and sometimes saving the children of Hinamizawa is my job.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:50.980
You're kind of like a mother.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.020
I'd rather have you call me onee-chan.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.160
Okay.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:03.110
Then, I'll be in your care, onee-chan.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.770
Nipah~

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:09.030
Damn, she's cute!

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.500
Where did you get lost, Rika-chan?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.540
I don't remember.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.030
I was exploring deep in the forest with Hanyuu,

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:22.920
then we said we'd play hide-and-seek.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:30.580
I climbed into a shrine, and when I came out again, things were different.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.730
An old shrine?

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:40.060
Maybe it's some kind of tunnel through time.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.560
This is Hinamizawa, right?

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:50.110
This is definitely Hinamizawa, though it may not be the Hinamizawa you remember.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.080
I'm sure you overcame space and time, and have arrived in the future!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:02.770
If I remember correctly, there was a huge fuss when we couldn't find you a long time ago.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:13.940
But because the you right here doesn't know that, I might be messing with consistency right now.

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:17.100
It's a time paradox ~nano desu!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.920
Time p-

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.060
It's fine if you don't understand.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.230
Let's go to that shrine first!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.730
It's not this one?

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.080
No, it's not.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:37.240
The shrine I climbed into had a tall thing next to it.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:43.750
But there are so many shrines in Hinamizawa.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.340
Is it this one?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.760
This isn't a shrine, but could this be it?

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.120
We're in trouble.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.520
If we don't know where to go, searching won't do us any good.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:08.020
I'm sorry for getting you into trouble, Onee-chan.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.290
How adorable!

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:15.950
The current Rika would never say that kind of thing to me.

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.790
Rika, this way!

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.550
Are you okay, Rika?

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:40.550
We're faster this way!

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.470
Nipah~

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:08.540
It's so warm!

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.000
We're lucky it was only a shower.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.210
We're safe now.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.800
But we can't just relax here.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:24.560
If the reincarnation of Oyashiro-sama is gone, the Hinamizawa of the past will be in trouble.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.640
I have to get her back before sunset.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.830
This brings me back to life!

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.390
It's nice that there's a place like this around.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:36.830
I wonder where Kei-chan went.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.850
We lost him on the way here.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:44.990
Let him be. If a boy were here, we couldn't be sitting around like this.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:49.580
Please wait just a second, I heard someone's voice from over there.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:52.580
What?

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:55.840
What are all of you doing here?

00:10:56.070 --> 00:11:01.750
We were done studying, so we tagged along with Satoko making traps.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.990
And then it suddenly started raining.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.600
Oh? Who is this?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.740
I'm taking you home with me!

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.350
At least wear something!

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:14.040
You're just too indiscriminate about things.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.550
I'm sorry, she's just too adorable.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.940
You're right about that.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.860
She's in the same league as Satoko and I.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:28.420
Onee-chan, you look a lot like me.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:31.850
We're distant relatives.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.150
And coincidentally, my name is Rika, too.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:37.210
Wow!

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.880
She's making it up as nonchalantly as usual.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.200
But Rika, I've never heard about you having such a relative.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.830
How come she's lost in a place like this?

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:51.690
What is this shrine you are looking for?

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.350
That's...

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.330
"That's"?

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.960
That's what we'll find out when we find the shrine.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.640
Nipah!

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.410
Nipah!

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:07.160
Nipah! Nipah!

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.160
Nipah!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.210
Isn't this just too suspicious?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.660
There must be a reason behind it.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.530
Who cares?

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:18.450
Let's help her out.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:23.450
In short, if it's cute, you're in. Right, Rena-san?

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:27.040
Wow, what a downpour.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.020
I need to take a bath, it's gonna warm me right up.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:35.190
Hi.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:39.840
What the hell are you showing us, Kei-chan?!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.790
You're misunderstanding, it's not like I...

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.020
There has to be a limit to your perversion!

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:46.700
Trap activation!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.520
Bullet punishment!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:57.130
Time to take Keiichi-kun's frankfurter home with me!

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:06.670
That shrine you are talking about is probably concealed.

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:08.720
Concealed?

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:14.710
I'm not entirely sure why, but some shrines were built where you can't easily find them.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:17.110
My grandmother told me about it.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:20.230
I wonder why that is.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.620
A concealed shrine?

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:26.790
I never knew there was that kind of place in Hinamizawa.

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:30.240
It's kind of mysterious.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.220
Does this area seem familiar?

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:34.130
Yes.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.870
I think it was this kind of place.

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:38.350
Speaking of which,

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:42.510
I once played hide-and-seek with you and got lost, right?

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:45.510
Yes, that was a long time ago, though.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:50.280
Back then, I was helped by a girl who looked just like you.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:54.090
I always thought it had been a dream, but it actually happened.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:54.770
There!

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:56.650
I'm sure this is it.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:04.150
What?

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.250
What is it?

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.400
It's gone.

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:13.410
The shrine isn't here.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.900
What?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:20.670
I'm certain there was a shrine here.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.890
Miii~

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.570
This isn't good.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:47.190
If I don't get back soon, Hanyuu will start to get worried.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:53.090
Rika, do you by any chance remember how you returned to the other world?

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:55.770
I have been trying to remember, as I told you before.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:58.960
But it has already been a hundred years...

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.710
I wonder what that could mean, I wonder.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.360
Is this what they call being spirited away?

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:08.690
Although the season doesn't match.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:12.370
But to be spirited away, a human has to disappear, right?

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.350
I have never heard of a building being taken.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.730
We have to get to the bottom of this phenomenon.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:23.170
There are strange things happening from time to time in Hinamizawa.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.360
What's wrong?

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:31.130
Everyone seems to be getting along well.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:34.120
It's different from the Hinamizawa I came from.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:41.960
Everyone argues about what to do with the dam.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:47.430
I hope that the Hinamizawa I came from will be able to become like this soon, as well.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:56.060
Looks like the Rika-chan over there is getting sleepy.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.820
I can't blame her.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:00.440
She's been trying to keep up with our pace all day.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:11.780
Sleep, sleep peacefully, my child.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:21.140
For you are a dear boy, a really good child. Enjoy thy slumber.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.910
I am feeling a bit sleepy now myself.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:23.640
We usually cause a stir, but days like this from time to time are nice, as well.

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:31.920
Little boy, bear in mind, whichever path you may take,

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:41.230
once we pass through the mountains, we shall be at the village.

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:46.230
Hanyuu, could you sing that song again?

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:50.070
Eh, but the Rika-chan over here is already asleep.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.160
It's okay already.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.780
If I tell you to sing, start singing!

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.190
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:59.140
Ehm... Ehm...

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:04.400
Sleep, sleep peacefully, my child.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:09.260
For you are a dear boy, a really good child. Enjoy thy slumber.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:14.290
Little boy, bear in mind, whichever path you may take.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:19.850
Should you lose your way, you may run into a demon.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.260
Those are some rare lyrics.

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:24.970
They seem different from the ones I know.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.690
The latter one was Hinamizawa's version.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:30.860
It's popular in this area.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:35.960
I know the Furude shrine also had hidden shrines built in the area.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:41.120
And I have also heard that this lullaby is a hint to the location of one.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.330
But I don't know the full details.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.820
And I seem to have forgotten, as well.

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:51.380
I see, so it's a code hidden in the lullaby.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.260
Then if we can understand the meaning of the lyrics...

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.760
...will we be able to find the shrine we are looking for?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.980
That is a possibility...

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:02.680
...if the shrine we're looking for is hidden.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.520
They certainly hold a deeper meaning.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.960
The verse says to be careful while passing through the mountains of the village,

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:11.770
or you shall lose your way and run into a demon.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.130
It sounds like some vague warning.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.930
With the part about running into a demon, implying a place to avoid.

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:21.660
In other words, it's a forbidden area.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:25.040
A place you would need permission to enter.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.300
Sister.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.300
Onee.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:26.700
Huh?

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:30.560
Did our grandma ever mention such a place during her conversations?

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:32.150
Hmm...

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:34.070
I was once on the verge of learning something,

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:38.890
when Ooishi-san and the police had a tea party at the place in Okinomiya.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:42.640
"Don't tell me you're going on a group date." is what she said.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.930
What could she be thinking in her age?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.960
Grandma, although looking like that, is a maiden at heart, you know!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.960
Grandma, old as she may be, is a maiden at heart, you know!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:52.350
A maiden? With that face? Lies!

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:53.820
Those two look alike.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:55.810
And the twins....

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:02.070
Rika, is there a map of Hinamizawa at the main shrine?

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:17.460
This is it!

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:19.760
This is the shrine we were at before.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:26.220
And there is a trail leading to another one here beyond the mountain path.

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:30.230
Twin shrines?

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.910
That's right, they are copies of each other.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:35.360
Looking at Mion and Shion gave me the idea of where it was.

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:37.650
Looking at us?

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.360
What do you mean by that?

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:41.580
The Lullaby's lyrics.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:47.190
In the first and second versions, the mountains might seem the same, but there are two different mountains.

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:49.870
That's why you would get lost on the way back.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.770
Look! This is the place we went to before.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:59.200
My mum was a fan of mystery novels, you see.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:02.260
She told me about that trick once.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:06.320
What if you wanted to hide something in a place others can't find?

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:08.010
What would you do?

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:13.050
You put a dummy where it can be easily seen.

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.420
I see.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:18.260
The twin exchange trick.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.910
This is the first time I've gone so far.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:28.150
We're at the outskirts of Hinamizawa by now.

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:30.540
It's only the mountain from here on.

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.620
It's the edge of the world.

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.150
For Hinamizawa, that is.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.300
There it is!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:50.460
How is it?

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:53.270
Is this the place you've been looking for?

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:00.140
That's right!

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:01.410
This is the place!

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:03.070
There's no mistake!

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:06.600
You did it!

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:08.580
Big thanks to your success, Keiichi-kun!

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.640
As expected of Kei-chan!

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:13.950
He's usually a pervert, but a dependable guy when needed.

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:17.070
Though he will probably revert back soon.

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:19.090
No, not that much...

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:23.600
Could this be something left by one of your bloodline?

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:28.850
They hid this shrine and the trigger out of sight, so they wouldn't be found.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.350
Hanyuu?

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.350
What's wrong, Hanyuu-chan?

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.810
I can't...

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.900
I don't want to return her.

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:47.710
Because I know that from here on she's going to go through much pain and suffering.

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:55.110
If I let her go back now, she'll only have to repeat those sad events again.

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:59.130
Rather than having it that way, keeping her is much better.

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:04.080
Onee-chan, are you crying?

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:08.180
Huh? What are you girls talking about?

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:10.450
Just keep quiet and watch.

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:19.770
Rika-chan.

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:26.400
Would you like to live here like Onee-chan said?

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:32.030
This Hinamizawa is peaceful, and everyone here lives happily.

00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:39.560
Wouldn't you like to live in this Hinamizawa?

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.550
No.

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:53.540
I shall return to my Hinamizawa.

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:57.220
I have an important job there.

00:22:57.220 --> 00:22:58.590
And besides...

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:05.070
...if I don't go back, I won't get to see Hanyuu any more.

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:09.570
Because I love Hanyuu a lot!

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:12.070
Nipah~

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.620
I've made it back!

00:24:26.280 --> 00:24:30.080
Thank you for all your help!

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:33.800
Um, will we be able to see each other again?

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:37.100
Of course!

00:24:37.100 --> 00:24:40.230
If you keep being a good girl and do your best for everyone's sake,

00:24:40.230 --> 00:24:42.890
I'm sure we'll be able to see each other again.

00:24:42.890 --> 00:24:44.240
Really?

00:24:45.660 --> 00:24:46.420
Yes.

00:24:46.420 --> 00:24:51.670
When your Hinamizawa becomes a wonderful place, we'll see each other again.

00:24:52.010 --> 00:24:53.130
That's why...

00:24:58.700 --> 00:24:59.750
That's why...

00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:01.750
Be strong!

00:25:01.750 --> 00:25:04.090
Yes, I will!

00:25:05.920 --> 00:25:10.440
Well, then, thank you for all of the help you've given me.

00:25:10.810 --> 00:25:15.340
I will be looking forward to meeting you all again.

00:25:10.810 --> 00:25:15.340
I can't wait to see you all again!

00:25:15.340 --> 00:25:17.270
Oh, yeah!

00:25:17.270 --> 00:25:18.200
Stay well!

00:25:18.200 --> 00:25:19.000
Do your best!

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:19.430
See you soon!

00:25:19.430 --> 00:25:20.260
Stay perky!

00:25:20.260 --> 00:25:20.990
Bye bye!

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:24.330
Hanyuu!

00:25:25.840 --> 00:25:27.330
Rika!

00:25:29.290 --> 00:25:31.460
I was so worried!

00:25:31.460 --> 00:25:33.280
I'm really sorry ~nano desu.

00:25:33.280 --> 00:25:35.940
Geez, where have you been?!

00:25:35.940 --> 00:25:37.320
Hinamizawa ~nano desu!

00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:39.770
I'm glad it worked out this way...

00:25:39.770 --> 00:25:41.000
Huh?

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:45.350
...and that things turned out the way they are now.

00:25:45.850 --> 00:25:50.450
I may have experienced many hardships, but thanks to them...

00:25:50.450 --> 00:25:53.680
...I can be together this way with everyone.

00:26:14.310 --> 00:26:17.100
It's just a regular shrine, right?

00:26:17.100 --> 00:26:19.970
I wonder if it was all a dream, I wonder.

00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:22.680
Oh my, what a coincidence that was.

00:26:22.680 --> 00:26:24.850
I was seeing the same dream.

00:26:24.850 --> 00:26:28.570
Is this one of Oyashiro-sama's mysterious powers?

00:26:28.570 --> 00:26:31.480
Rika-chan, the child from just now...

00:26:36.210 --> 00:26:40.980
Don't worry about her, I'm sure she will manage everything just fine.

00:26:40.980 --> 00:26:41.990
Rika...

00:26:41.990 --> 00:26:46.280
That's because she has Hanyuu by her side.

00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:48.070
Nipah~

00:26:56.720 --> 00:26:59.410
It really becomes cool as the evening approaches.

00:26:59.410 --> 00:27:02.760
The cicadas are chirping loudly as well.

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:07.220
Can you guys come over to our place for dinner tonight?

00:27:07.220 --> 00:27:10.140
Oh, it's been a while since I had your home-made cooking, Satoko.

00:27:10.390 --> 00:27:12.270
I'm coming, as well!

00:27:10.840 --> 00:27:11.820
You better eat a lot.

00:27:11.820 --> 00:27:13.110
I'll take you up on your offer.

00:27:12.270 --> 00:27:15.020
Yeah! Cook us a feast!

00:27:13.110 --> 00:27:14.330
It's gonna be nice.

00:27:15.410 --> 00:27:17.420
Let's get going.

00:27:30.050 --> 00:27:31.290
Hanyuu?

00:27:33.040 --> 00:27:35.270
Let's go back, Hanyuu.

00:27:35.270 --> 00:27:37.050
To our home.

00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:40.800
Okay ~nano desu!

00:28:03.660 --> 00:28:08.100
The person who lost is 'It'. You're going to get caught! (This way or that?)

00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:13.250
A heart-racing dream that I just can't awaken from. Longer than eternity.

00:28:21.340 --> 00:28:26.110
One man's trash is another man's treasure.

00:28:26.110 --> 00:28:30.270
So when everything seems lost, talk it out with everyone.

00:28:30.270 --> 00:28:32.600
I just can't wait until it's time to go home.

00:28:32.600 --> 00:28:35.090
Today's snack is cream puffs! ~nano desu

00:28:35.090 --> 00:28:40.710
Even if we'll just be messing about, it's time for a special transformation!

00:28:40.710 --> 00:28:45.290
The person who lost is 'It'. You're going to get caught! (This way or that?)

00:28:45.290 --> 00:28:49.470
A heart-racing dream that I just can't awaken from. Longer than eternity.

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:54.820
The key is a heart that believes.

00:28:56.180 --> 00:29:00.730
We'll have the courage to fight troubles never seen before

00:29:00.730 --> 00:29:03.090
if we combine our powers.

00:29:03.090 --> 00:29:05.190
So let's change it, with a miracle!

00:29:05.190 --> 00:29:09.650
Even if we're reckless, and tomorrow seems a little bit far off,

00:29:09.650 --> 00:29:12.100
the diversions we take today...

00:29:12.100 --> 00:29:14.440
...will make us shine more than anyone. (Yes!)

00:29:14.440 --> 00:29:16.580
Our chance! (Auau~)

00:29:16.580 --> 00:29:18.810
Our dream! (Nano desu~)

00:29:18.810 --> 00:29:24.700
A time begins where we have surpassed ourselves.
